1
00:01:21,397 --> 00:01:25,344
نَسْعَلُ اللهَ عَزُّوْاَجَلْ أَلَّا يَدَعْ بَيْنَ نَا وَلَا فِيْنَا،،

2
00:01:27,211 --> 00:01:32,439
اَحَدً اِلَّا بِذَنْبٍ مَغْفُوْرْ وَسَاعٍ مَشْكُوْرْ

3
00:01:33,674 --> 00:01:41,366
 وَنَسْعَلُ اللهَ عَزُّوْاَجَلْ أَنْ َيَجْعَلَنَامِنْ كُلِّ هَماٍ فَرَجَا وَمِنْ كُلِّ ضِيْقٍ مَخْرَجَا وَمِنْ كُلِّ عُسْرٍيُسْرَاَ

4
00:01:47,002 --> 00:01:51,231
We talked about the, attention Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين)

5
00:01:51,650 --> 00:01:55,029
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه  gave to a Ibadaat(عبادات),

6
00:01:56,615 --> 00:01:59,300
we talked about the importance he gave to Salaat(صلاة)

7
00:02:00,202 --> 00:02:05,671
and we missed the part on Taraweh(تراويح), we start with that.

8
00:02:09,133 --> 00:02:13,914
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه came into the Masjid(مسجد) in Ramadan(رمضان),

9
00:02:15,992 --> 00:02:20,112
and he found them scattered around the Masjid(مسجد).

10
00:02:22,907 --> 00:02:25,405
This man is praying on his own,

11
00:02:26,651 --> 00:02:30,918
this man is leading a Jama'at(جماعة) of  three or four or five.

12
00:02:31,274 --> 00:02:36,087
This one is leading a Jama'at(جماعة) of 10, this one is alone, all over the Masjid(مسجد).

13
00:02:37,495 --> 00:02:40,530
And there Qira'at(قرأة ) was confusing each other.

14
00:02:43,143 --> 00:02:52,605
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه said: "I will combine them all, behind one Imam(اِمَام)."

15
00:02:54,087 --> 00:02:57,925
Rather than have everyone do their own thing, let them all pray together.

16
00:03:00,732 --> 00:03:06,692
So, he appointed Obaeye Bin Ka'abرضي الله عنه, the scholar of Qur'an, the Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

17
00:03:07,303 --> 00:03:12,144
from the people of Madina to lead Salaat-Ut-Taraweeh(صلاة التراويح).

18
00:03:15,647 --> 00:03:26,454
He came the next day and he saw the Muslims praying in Jama'at(جماعة) in cohesion, so he said;

19
00:03:26,919 --> 00:03:31,312
نِعْمَتِ الْبِدْعَةْ هَذِهِ، اَوْ نِعْمَ الْبِدْعَ هَذِهِ

20
00:03:31,865 --> 00:03:36,777
This is a good Bid'ah( بدعة), this is a good Bid'ah( بدعة).

21
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:45,535
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was happy to see that the Muslims are now praying together

22
00:03:45,575 --> 00:03:49,232
rather than the disorganized way, it was happening before in the Masjid(مسجد)

23
00:03:51,285 --> 00:03:58,257
and this quote by Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه , is mentioned frequently

24
00:03:59,098 --> 00:04:04,764
and it's always brought up as an evidence to support,

25
00:04:05,604 --> 00:04:09,382
whenever someone or somebody would do something new in religion.

26
00:04:12,029 --> 00:04:15,754
So, is it truly a Bid'ah( بدعة)?

27
00:04:16,953 --> 00:04:20,318
Did Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) really innovate?

28
00:04:20,995 --> 00:04:31,043
Or he was speaking in a figurative sense, that this is something good that's what he meant.

29
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:34,666
Well let's look at the history of Salah-At-Taraweeh(صلاة التراويح).

30
00:04:34,822 --> 00:04:39,304
Is Salah-At-Taraweeh(صلاة التراويح) something that was started by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) or did it exist before?

31
00:04:41,294 --> 00:04:46,358
In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ some would pray at home

32
00:04:46,413 --> 00:04:47,526
 and some would pray in the Masjid(مسجد).

33
00:04:47,641 --> 00:04:51,681
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came into the Masjid(مسجد) in Ramadan(رمضان) and he started praying.

34
00:04:52,673 --> 00:04:55,584
The Sahabah(صحابه) who were there obviously joined Rasool Allah ﷺ.

35
00:04:56,463 --> 00:05:00,314
So, it was a Jama'at(جماعة) of Salah-At-Taraweeh(صلاة التراويح), in the Masjid(مسجد),

36
00:05:01,715 --> 00:05:05,252
the next day more people poured in.

37
00:05:06,926 --> 00:05:10,725
The third day more people, the fourth day the Masjid(مسجد) was packed.

38
00:05:13,155 --> 00:05:15,596
Rasool Allah ﷺ on the fifth day didn't show up.

39
00:05:17,405 --> 00:05:20,123
And then he told the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

40
00:05:20,148 --> 00:05:23,842
أَمَّا بَعْدََ فَإِنَه’ لَمْ يَخْفَ عَلَيَّ مَكَانَكُمْ

41
00:05:24,001 --> 00:05:27,989
وَلَكِنِّيْ خَشِيْتُ أَنْ تُفْرَضَ عَلَيْكُمْ فَتَعْجَزُوْا عَنْهَا

42
00:05:30,438 --> 00:05:35,335
I did not want this to become a mandatory Salah(صلاة) on you.

43
00:05:36,519 --> 00:05:40,415
What will happen, if Rasool Allah ﷺ keeps praying it in the Masjid(مسجد) as a Jama'at(جماعة)

44
00:05:40,462 --> 00:05:42,468
 and Sahabah(صحابه) are joining him all the time?

45
00:05:42,901 --> 00:05:46,761
It would turn into something that is mandatory

46
00:05:47,492 --> 00:05:52,343
and Rasool Allah ﷺ wants Taraweeh(التراويح) to remain as a voluntary act.

47
00:05:53,039 --> 00:05:56,604
So, he said that's why I stopped leading the Salah(صلاة) in the Masjid(مسجد)

48
00:05:56,797 --> 00:05:59,082
not because leading it in Jama'ah(جماعة) was wrong

49
00:05:59,231 --> 00:06:02,223
but because I don't want it to become mandatory on you.

50
00:06:03,879 --> 00:06:08,315
Therefore, Salah-At-Taraweeh(صلاة التراويح) existed in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

51
00:06:11,546 --> 00:06:15,923
So, what Umar(عُمَر) did was, revived something that was already there.

52
00:06:17,351 --> 00:06:21,762
He just revived, something that was already done by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

53
00:06:24,324 --> 00:06:27,722
Because even in the time Umar(عُمَر) Jama'aat(جماعات) were happening

54
00:06:27,747 --> 00:06:29,749
but there were more than one Jama'ah(جماعة), they were scattered around.

55
00:06:29,773 --> 00:06:30,993
So, he wanted to bring them,

56
00:06:31,105 --> 00:06:36,838
so basically what Umar(عُمَر) did was combined the Jama'aat(جماعات) into one Jama'ah(جماعة), that's all.

57
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:43,851
So, this cannot be used as evidence that you're allowed to invent things in Sharia(شريعة)

58
00:06:44,586 --> 00:06:49,360
but you are allowed to improve the way things are happening,

59
00:06:49,571 --> 00:06:54,343
within the boundaries of the Sharia(شريعة), not to change anything in Shariah(شريعة).

60
00:06:54,368 --> 00:06:57,013
But to improve the way, you practice it.

61
00:06:58,287 --> 00:07:02,177
For example, we are praying in our Masajid(مساجد) Salaat-Ul-Jama'at(صلاة جماعة).

62
00:07:02,396 --> 00:07:07,455
All right, we added an improvement to that and that's now we're using loudspeakers

63
00:07:07,479 --> 00:07:11,545
something that they didn't use in the old days, we have the Mics, we have the speakers,

64
00:07:11,936 --> 00:07:14,421
it is to improve our Salah(صلاة) of Jama'at(جماعة)

65
00:07:14,796 --> 00:07:18,144
to make it easier to make it more beneficial for the people.

66
00:07:18,288 --> 00:07:21,781
We didn't really change anything in the format of the Salah(صلاة) itself.

67
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:26,861
We just added something to it that is not actually a part of the Ibadah(عبادة)

68
00:07:27,614 --> 00:07:30,965
and that is something that is absolutely legal and allowed.

69
00:07:31,679 --> 00:07:35,002
You can call it an innovation, but it's not an innovation in religion.

70
00:07:36,796 --> 00:07:39,245
So, I hope that the concept is clear.

71
00:07:41,999 --> 00:07:49,627
We'll move on to the next section, and that is the economic crisis that occurred

72
00:07:49,881 --> 00:07:52,450
during the time of  Umar Bin  Khattab رضي الله عنه .

73
00:07:57,770 --> 00:08:02,733
And this is called Aam-Er-Ramadah(عام الرمادة), the year of the Ramadah(الرمادة), the Ashes.

74
00:08:06,198 --> 00:08:11,370
And this was the 18th year of Hijrah(هجرة),

75
00:08:11,588 --> 00:08:15,709
a few years into the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of  Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه,

76
00:08:18,157 --> 00:08:29,823
the sky withheld its rain, and the Arabian Peninsula sunk into a famine.

77
00:08:32,041 --> 00:08:35,296
They were dependent on the scars rain that they receive.

78
00:08:35,706 --> 00:08:37,837
And they didn't receive anything that year.

79
00:08:39,747 --> 00:08:46,727
So, it was said that wild beasts were so hungry they started attacking humans,

80
00:08:48,593 --> 00:08:58,018
the cattle that the Arabs or the tribes owned were dying.

81
00:08:59,632 --> 00:09:05,726
They would say a man would have this goat and it is so skinny, so he would slaughter it,

82
00:09:06,377 --> 00:09:09,863
and would barely be able to eat it, because it's so disgusting.

83
00:09:13,278 --> 00:09:20,774
And the Bedouins started coming in flocks to Madina

84
00:09:22,718 --> 00:09:27,526
to come to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه asking him for help,

85
00:09:27,921 --> 00:09:29,717
and Umar(عُمَر) has nothing to give them.

86
00:09:32,356 --> 00:09:39,084
So, you have these refugees in Madina, thousands of them,

87
00:09:39,868 --> 00:09:46,299
the count was 60,000, Bedouins who flocked to Madina.

88
00:09:46,324 --> 00:09:49,263
And when we say 60,000 in those days, that's a huge number.

89
00:09:50,169 --> 00:09:54,150
Keep in mind that the population of the earth at that time was very low.

90
00:09:55,528 --> 00:09:58,850
Possibly didn't reached the billion mark yet.

91
00:10:00,842 --> 00:10:03,659
So, the population was very scars.

92
00:10:03,708 --> 00:10:09,023
So, you have 60,000 in those days, it means a lot, in today's terms.

93
00:10:09,831 --> 00:10:15,257
And all of these refugees were coming to Madina thinking that the Khalifah(خليفه) has a solution for them.

94
00:10:15,496 --> 00:10:17,541
And the Khalifah(خليفه) was as hungry as they are…

95
00:10:20,601 --> 00:10:31,712
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was having this meal with a Bedouin.

96
00:10:33,315 --> 00:10:39,686
He had for him crushed bread in butter.

97
00:10:42,163 --> 00:10:44,495
So, he is eating with this Bedouin.

98
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:48,712
So, the Bedouin would take the piece of bread

99
00:10:50,071 --> 00:10:58,604
and he would pass it on the rim of the plate, to wipe all of the butter that is stuck to the plate

100
00:10:59,869 --> 00:11:00,444
and he would eat.

101
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:08,279
He would take the next piece of bread and pass it along the rim to absorb all of the butter in there

102
00:11:10,189 --> 00:11:12,002
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is watching him.

103
00:11:13,862 --> 00:11:19,193
And then he said: It seems that you haven't had any butter for some time.

104
00:11:21,356 --> 00:11:26,600
The man said: Yes, Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), I never had butter or oil.

105
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:30,771
And I never saw anybody eat it for a very, very long time.

106
00:11:32,388 --> 00:11:37,211
He was so hungry…. and, and butter was part of their diet, see

107
00:11:38,458 --> 00:11:47,354
animal shortening, or oil that comes from vegetable or vegetable sources, such as

108
00:11:47,681 --> 00:11:50,914
olives, or other seed, that they would grind,

109
00:11:50,954 --> 00:11:53,485
Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) what type of oil that they would have in that time.

110
00:11:53,565 --> 00:11:57,832
But definitely, they had olive oil, which was an integral part of their diet

111
00:11:58,713 --> 00:12:06,306
because of poverty and because the amount that they would eat was so low, your body needs fat, you know, now

112
00:12:06,578 --> 00:12:10,800
because we eat so much, everybody tells us that fat is not good for you,

113
00:12:10,824 --> 00:12:13,180
fat is not good for you, you're not supposed to have any fat.

114
00:12:13,498 --> 00:12:18,006
However, you're supposed to have about 20% fat in your diet.

115
00:12:19,666 --> 00:12:22,723
That's the right amount of fat that you should have in your diet.

116
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:25,142
The thing is, because we're having so much of it,

117
00:12:25,252 --> 00:12:27,460
the physicians are telling us to stay away from it.

118
00:12:27,777 --> 00:12:33,546
In those days, because they were having so less of it, they had to eat more

119
00:12:33,824 --> 00:12:37,304
their bodies needed that fat because you have to have fat in your body.

120
00:12:40,988 --> 00:12:46,164
So, for them olive oil and fat was an important part of their diet.

121
00:12:46,188 --> 00:12:51,852
This man is saying that I haven't seen fat or oil in a very, very long time.

122
00:12:54,498 --> 00:12:57,837
When Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه saw that, he made an oath

123
00:12:58,134 --> 00:13:05,966
that he is not going to taste meat, butter.

124
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:15,165
He's not gonna taste it, until the Ummah(امة) eats it and the historian say;

125
00:13:15,189 --> 00:13:19,546
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, stuck to his word and fulfilled his oath.

126
00:13:20,211 --> 00:13:25,586
And until he made sure that the Ummah(امة) are having sufficient amount of food

127
00:13:25,961 --> 00:13:27,894
that is when he started eating it again.

128
00:13:34,324 --> 00:13:34,981
He used to say;

129
00:13:35,019 --> 00:13:39,933
كَيْفَ يَعْنِيْنِيْ شَئْنُ الرَّعِيَّهْ إِذَا لَمْ يَمَسَّنِيْ مَا يَمَسُّهُمْ

130
00:13:40,557 --> 00:13:47,040
How can I be concerned with my people, if I don't go through what they're going,

131
00:13:48,284 --> 00:13:51,225
I need to feel their pain, I need to feel their suffering.

132
00:13:51,721 --> 00:13:54,114
And that's why after you fast the month of Ramadan(رمضان),

133
00:13:54,252 --> 00:13:58,118
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells you to give the Zakaat-Ul-Fitr(زكواة الفطر) Sadaqat tul fitr(صدقه الفطر)

134
00:13:58,862 --> 00:14:03,487
because you have experienced the hunger that the poor go through.

135
00:14:03,655 --> 00:14:10,905
So, you finish your fasting with giving out food to make them happy on the Day of Eid.

136
00:14:14,486 --> 00:14:19,106
 The Sahabah(صحابه) used to say that the color of the face of Umar(عُمَر) changed

137
00:14:19,455 --> 00:14:20,577
in the year of Ramadah(رمادة).

138
00:14:21,069 --> 00:14:25,373
It became very dark and thin because of the food that he was eating,

139
00:14:25,974 --> 00:14:29,207
he restricted his diet to dry bread

140
00:14:29,668 --> 00:14:35,222
Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) how old it is and he would dip it in oil or vinegar

141
00:14:35,605 --> 00:14:38,932
and that's all he would have, no meat, no butter.

142
00:14:39,514 --> 00:14:42,696
You can see that it's a very limited diet and it's unhealthy

143
00:14:43,389 --> 00:14:45,675
and that's why the body of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) changed

144
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:48,966
and the color of his face changed to the extent that Aslam(أسلم) said;

145
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:55,279
كُنَّا نَقُوْلُ لَوْ لَمْ يَرْفَهْ الله عزوجل اَلْمَحَلَّهْ عَامَ الرَّمَادَهْ

146
00:14:55,490 --> 00:14:58,986
لَظَنَنَّا أَنَّا عُمر يَمُوْتُوْ هَمًّا بِاَمْرِالْمُسْلِمِيْنَ

147
00:15:00,039 --> 00:15:05,808
Aslam(أسلم) said: We used to think that if Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ did not elevate

148
00:15:06,226 --> 00:15:10,724
the hunger of the year of Ramadah(رمادة), Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would have died

149
00:15:11,471 --> 00:15:13,328
because of his concern for his people.

150
00:15:14,411 --> 00:15:18,829
He wouldn't be able to carry on long in that fashion,

151
00:15:19,067 --> 00:15:20,230
he would have died,

152
00:15:21,063 --> 00:15:25,815
but it was the blessing of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that it only lasted for a year and then it was lifted.

153
00:15:29,359 --> 00:15:35,278
He was very strict even with his children, he saw his young child, one of his boys,

154
00:15:35,938 --> 00:15:40,787
having some fruit in his hand, one piece of fruit Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

155
00:15:40,811 --> 00:15:44,958
بَخِنْ بَخِنْ  اِبْنِ اَمِيْرُ الْمُومِنِيْنَ يَأْ كُلُوْ بِتِّيْخَ

156
00:15:46,045 --> 00:15:50,891
The son of Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) is eating fruits, while the Muslims are hungry

157
00:15:51,497 --> 00:15:55,601
and he wanted to take that fruit from his son and the son just ran away,

158
00:15:55,665 --> 00:15:57,371
his child just ran away and he was just crying.

159
00:15:58,368 --> 00:16:02,042
You know, the child was crying, my father wants to take away from me this fruit,

160
00:16:04,343 --> 00:16:07,948
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), that's very difficult on a father to do.

161
00:16:08,452 --> 00:16:11,284
And he's pursuing this child, he wants to take it away from him.

162
00:16:11,443 --> 00:16:14,845
Until, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was told that your child actually bought it.

163
00:16:15,185 --> 00:16:18,239
With a handful of Nawah(نواة), date seeds.

164
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:26,466
So, actually he bought it, otherwise Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would have taken that fruit from his son.

165
00:16:27,774 --> 00:16:31,099
So, he even place restrictions on his family.

166
00:16:31,139 --> 00:16:36,193
Yani(يعني) it was very difficult for you to turn down your children when you know they're hungry

167
00:16:36,233 --> 00:16:37,590
and they want something to eat,

168
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:41,825
you know, you would give them the best, you would prefer them over yourself.

169
00:16:42,681 --> 00:16:46,920
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) here is trying to take away, snatch away that fruit from his young child.

170
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:49,752
And with children, you know, they don't understand this,

171
00:16:49,776 --> 00:16:51,892
this child was crying, was weeping.

172
00:16:53,608 --> 00:16:56,538
And he had to run away and then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was stopped

173
00:16:56,563 --> 00:16:59,266
and they told him that he actually bought it, so let him have it.

174
00:17:01,718 --> 00:17:10,310
So, he applied the same rules that would apply to the rest of Ummah(امة), on himself.

175
00:17:10,605 --> 00:17:12,821
And he lived the way they were living.

176
00:17:13,249 --> 00:17:15,179
They're not eating butter, I'm not gonna have butter,

177
00:17:15,219 --> 00:17:17,306
they're not eating meat, I'm not gonna have meat.

178
00:17:20,178 --> 00:17:23,568
And by the way, this wasn't the condition on over the Muslim world.

179
00:17:23,593 --> 00:17:25,040
This was just in the Arabian Peninsula.

180
00:17:25,490 --> 00:17:29,492
The rest of the Muslim world, were not really affected by this,

181
00:17:29,539 --> 00:17:33,934
I mean history books tells us that this was something confined to the Arabian Peninsula.

182
00:17:39,730 --> 00:17:41,876
We mentioned the refugee camps.

183
00:17:42,439 --> 00:17:46,514
So, they opened up camps for the refugees 60,000 in total,

184
00:17:46,987 --> 00:17:54,481
almost two thirds of them died because of hunger and diseases.

185
00:17:55,317 --> 00:17:59,359
First of all these Bedouins are not used to the climate of Madina.

186
00:17:59,818 --> 00:18:02,613
They come from a very pure and pristine environment.

187
00:18:02,653 --> 00:18:04,331
The desert is very clean and pure.

188
00:18:04,950 --> 00:18:17,585
You know, for example, you would find that the lowest ratio, or existence of germs and bacteria is in deserts

189
00:18:17,690 --> 00:18:20,047
because nothing can really live it's very dry and hot,

190
00:18:20,684 --> 00:18:23,783
so it doesn't support these forms of life.

191
00:18:24,582 --> 00:18:27,384
So, it's a very healthy environment is very tough and difficult.

192
00:18:27,813 --> 00:18:28,852
But it's healthy,

193
00:18:29,653 --> 00:18:35,379
while in Madina you have in those days they were swamps in Madina because it was agricultural land.

194
00:18:35,604 --> 00:18:38,663
So, there were swamps and there was Hummah(همًا) in Madina.

195
00:18:38,688 --> 00:18:43,370
And some scholars would interpret it today as breakouts of malaria

196
00:18:44,686 --> 00:18:48,870
because it says in the books of history, it was a fever that would always break out in Madina,

197
00:18:49,116 --> 00:18:52,279
so they would say that it was possibly malaria because of the swamps

198
00:18:52,655 --> 00:18:55,638
that were in Madina because of the farm land.

199
00:18:56,244 --> 00:18:58,652
So, Madina wasn't a healthy environment.

200
00:18:58,714 --> 00:19:03,187
Even the the Muhajiroon( مهاجرون) when they came from Makkah to Madina they all fell ill

201
00:19:03,556 --> 00:19:08,886
and we know of the poetry of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Bilal Ibn Rabah رضي الله عنهم,

202
00:19:09,183 --> 00:19:13,366
when they were feeling home sick, they wanted to go back to Makkah

203
00:19:13,613 --> 00:19:22,729
because of the epidemic climate that existed in Madina and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

204
00:19:22,905 --> 00:19:26,621
أَللَّهُمَّ حَبِّبْ إِلَيْنَا الْمَدِيْنَهْ كَحُبِّنَا المَكَّهْ أَوْ أَشَدَّ حُبَّا

205
00:19:27,444 --> 00:19:31,718
O Allah make us love Madina, like we love Makkah or more

206
00:19:31,938 --> 00:19:34,955
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) suddenly all of the Sahabah(صحابه) loved Madina more than Makkah

207
00:19:36,524 --> 00:19:39,667
and that became their choice of residence

208
00:19:39,961 --> 00:19:41,928
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر), Uthman(عثمان), Ali(علي)

209
00:19:42,302 --> 00:19:45,095
they could have went back to Makkah, when Makkah was opened

210
00:19:45,135 --> 00:19:46,508
 but they chose to stay in Madina,

211
00:19:47,975 --> 00:19:49,569
when they disliked it, in the beginning.

212
00:19:50,459 --> 00:19:55,884
They didn't want to be in Madina, they were all singing these lines of poetry longing to go back to Makkah

213
00:19:56,185 --> 00:20:00,313
but because of the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ every Mo'min(مؤمن) today loves Madina.

214
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:09,517
Abu Hurairah رضى الله عنه said: May Allah have mercy on Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

215
00:20:09,771 --> 00:20:11,523
 I saw him the year of Ramadah(رمادة).

216
00:20:12,395 --> 00:20:18,435
By the way the meaning of Ramadah(رمادة) when I said ashes, it was so hot and dry

217
00:20:18,808 --> 00:20:22,767
 that when the wind is blowing in your face, it is as if it's blowing ashes in your face

218
00:20:22,839 --> 00:20:24,504
so that's why they called it Aam-Er-Ramadah(عام الرمادة).

219
00:20:25,998 --> 00:20:29,676
So, Abu Hurairah(أبوهريره) said: I saw him carrying two sacks on his back

220
00:20:30,341 --> 00:20:35,015
and oil in his hand, and he's carrying it to the refugee camps.

221
00:20:35,336 --> 00:20:37,964
And then he saw me, he said: Where did it come from Abu Hurairah(أبوهريره).

222
00:20:37,988 --> 00:20:39,370
He said: Not from far away.

223
00:20:40,259 --> 00:20:42,342
And then I joined in to help him.

224
00:20:42,771 --> 00:20:46,398
So, we went and saw a new group that just came in,

225
00:20:46,422 --> 00:20:48,519
they were 20 of them from the tribe of Muharib(محارب).

226
00:20:49,642 --> 00:20:51,425
So, Umar(عُمَر) asked them: Why did they come?

227
00:20:51,488 --> 00:20:55,282
They said: Al-Juhud(ألجحد), hunger brought us

228
00:20:56,296 --> 00:21:06,851
and then they pulled out roasted leather of dead animals that they were eating,

229
00:21:08,316 --> 00:21:12,174
they would rip off the leather from dead animals and eat it.

230
00:21:13,850 --> 00:21:15,613
They would cook that leather and eat it.

231
00:21:16,074 --> 00:21:17,779
That was how hungry they were.

232
00:21:18,782 --> 00:21:20,334
 And they would crush bones.

233
00:21:20,694 --> 00:21:24,958
So, they showed us this white powder, Crushed bones that, they would just swallow.

234
00:21:26,101 --> 00:21:27,333
That was how hungry they were!

235
00:21:28,413 --> 00:21:33,473
when they showed that to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he took off his Ridaah(رداع),

236
00:21:34,419 --> 00:21:40,580
and he started cooking for them, until they were full.

237
00:21:42,617 --> 00:21:43,811
Malik Bin Al-Aos(مالك بن ألأوس) he says:

238
00:21:43,836 --> 00:21:49,826
لَمَّا كَانَ عَامِ الرَّمَادَةْ قَدِمَ عُمر عَلى قَوْمِيْ وَهُمْ مِئَةْ بَيْتَ، فَنَزَلُوا الْجَبَّانَةْ

239
00:21:50,063 --> 00:21:56,396
فَكَانَ عُمر: يُطْعِمُ النَاسَ مَنْ جَاءَه’ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَأْتِ أَرْسَلَ اِلَيْهِ الدَّقِيْقَ وَالتَّمْرُ وَالْأَدْمُ إِلَى  مَنْزِلِهْ

240
00:21:57,046 --> 00:22:00,066
Malik Bin Aos(مالك بن ألأوس) he said: Umar(عُمَر) came to our camp

241
00:22:01,049 --> 00:22:02,946
and he provided us with food

242
00:22:03,343 --> 00:22:12,645
and the ones who did not come, he sent to them dates and flour and bread, he would send it out to them.

243
00:22:13,491 --> 00:22:16,340
فَكَانَ يُرْسِلُ إِلَى قَوْمِيْ بِمَا يُصْلِحُهُمْ شَهْرًا بِشَهْرَا,

244
00:22:16,370 --> 00:22:18,419
And He رضي الله عنه would send enough rations for a month

245
00:22:19,554 --> 00:22:25,058
and he would also visit the ill among them and he would provide the coffins to the dead.

246
00:22:25,973 --> 00:22:32,063
And Malik Bin Aos(مالك بن ألأوس) said that death was spreading like wildfire among our people.

247
00:22:32,846 --> 00:22:36,706
At one particular moment, I saw Umar(عُمَر) praying Janazah(جنازة) on 10 bodies.

248
00:22:39,027 --> 00:22:46,596
And when the famine was over, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told them: Go back to your land.

249
00:22:47,011 --> 00:22:49,315
 And I will provide you with transportation.

250
00:22:49,596 --> 00:22:53,419
And he ensured that everyone reached home safely.

251
00:22:55,187 --> 00:22:57,434
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), you know all of this work.

252
00:22:57,488 --> 00:23:01,361
This is very time consuming how would Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) do it.

253
00:23:01,733 --> 00:23:06,366
They would say: He would pray Ishaa(عشاء), go back home and start Qiyaam-Ul-Lail(قيا م اليل),

254
00:23:06,390 --> 00:23:12,859
praying, praying, praying, and then he would go and make his nightly patrols visiting these camps

255
00:23:13,168 --> 00:23:14,674
 and then he would spend the day with them.

256
00:23:15,266 --> 00:23:21,162
That was his schedule, it wasn't the nine to five job, it was 24/7.

257
00:23:31,051 --> 00:23:39,299
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sent letters to the different Muslim states,

258
00:23:39,912 --> 00:23:45,929
Egypt, Iraq, Ash-Sham(ألشام), asking for urgent emergency help.

259
00:23:46,971 --> 00:23:49,059
Because the problem was in the Arabian Peninsula.

260
00:23:49,639 --> 00:23:51,012
He sent a letter to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

261
00:23:51,099 --> 00:23:57,517
He said: You See me and my people dying and you and your people are enjoying the luxuries of life.

262
00:23:58,151 --> 00:23:59,784
فَوَا غَوْثَاهْ وَا غَوْثَاهْ,

263
00:23:59,987 --> 00:24:01,521
Help me fast, help me fast.

264
00:24:03,431 --> 00:24:05,717
See, the problem happened in Arabia

265
00:24:06,256 --> 00:24:15,336
and it became so bad that now people were dying and there was a time lag.

266
00:24:15,431 --> 00:24:18,238
Yes! Things are going to start coming from the other states but

267
00:24:18,489 --> 00:24:22,008
the problem was already so bad in Arabia that many people were dying.

268
00:24:22,715 --> 00:24:24,162
 See, that was the problem.

269
00:24:24,733 --> 00:24:27,128
 Things were fine in Egypt and Iraq and Ash-Sham(ألشام)

270
00:24:27,313 --> 00:24:31,848
but by the time the help came in, many people already died.

271
00:24:33,610 --> 00:24:36,210
And in those days they didn't have weather forecast, to tell them

272
00:24:36,235 --> 00:24:39,459
that rain is not going to come for months, so you can plan for it.

273
00:24:39,679 --> 00:24:43,078
It was something that just happened and they have to plan on the spot

274
00:24:43,855 --> 00:24:47,166
so he sends this letter to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) asking for urgent help.

275
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,289
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) sent him a letter back and said;

276
00:24:49,313 --> 00:24:50,237
أتاك الغوث

277
00:24:50,476 --> 00:24:51,776
Help is on its way.

278
00:24:53,834 --> 00:24:55,389
Help is on its way!

279
00:24:55,508 --> 00:25:01,193
 I will send you caravans the front will be in Madina and the end of it will be in Egypt

280
00:25:03,209 --> 00:25:06,645
 and he sends him a caravan of a 1000 camels loaded,

281
00:25:07,032 --> 00:25:08,797
he sends him 20 ships loaded

282
00:25:09,074 --> 00:25:16,560
and he send them 5000 garments that was the help or aid that came from Egypt

283
00:25:17,361 --> 00:25:20,884
 and then from Iraq he received 1000 camels,

284
00:25:21,521 --> 00:25:26,636
Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(ابوعبيدة عمرو بن جراح) sent him 4000 loaded camels,

285
00:25:27,586 --> 00:25:31,577
so when Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) came to Madina, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) appointed him

286
00:25:33,709 --> 00:25:37,186
to distribute all of the aid that came from Syria.

287
00:25:38,077 --> 00:25:40,577
So, Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) he distributed it

288
00:25:41,030 --> 00:25:47,116
and then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) gave him 40,000 Dirham(درهم), he gave it to him,

289
00:25:47,449 --> 00:25:49,159
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) refused to accept these,

290
00:25:49,183 --> 00:25:50,830
he said: We're fine, we're okay, we don't need it.

291
00:25:51,570 --> 00:25:54,038
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him: Take it. He said: I don't want it.

292
00:25:55,773 --> 00:26:02,126
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ offered me such money when I didn't need it or want it,

293
00:26:03,759 --> 00:26:05,874
but then Rasool Allah ﷺ told me: To take it.

294
00:26:06,807 --> 00:26:08,382
So, I'm telling you to take it.

295
00:26:09,025 --> 00:26:11,596
As long as you're not looking forward to that money,

296
00:26:11,846 --> 00:26:14,520
as long as your heart is not attached to this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

297
00:26:14,776 --> 00:26:17,467
if Halal(حلال) money comes to you, accept it.

298
00:26:18,466 --> 00:26:23,266
So, he gave it to Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) as a gift and a reward for his efforts.

299
00:26:23,301 --> 00:26:25,211
Even though Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) said: I don't need it.

300
00:26:26,083 --> 00:26:27,867
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) was willing to volunteer.

301
00:26:28,030 --> 00:26:30,703
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to pay him for his efforts.

302
00:26:32,186 --> 00:26:36,128
Muawiyah Bin Abi Sufiyan( معاويه بن ابي سفيان), sent 3000 camels,

303
00:26:36,390 --> 00:26:40,713
so now the pain and suffering was being elevated.

304
00:26:41,078 --> 00:26:43,747
However, as I said: Many people already died

305
00:26:44,790 --> 00:26:48,341
but because of the aid that was coming in, things were improving.

306
00:26:50,462 --> 00:26:54,033
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: If this famine would extend

307
00:26:55,076 --> 00:26:59,978
I would put every hungry person with somebody who is wealthy

308
00:27:00,467 --> 00:27:05,045
because people don't die on a half full stomach.

309
00:27:06,831 --> 00:27:12,260
If somebody is having a full meal, I will pair them with somebody who has having nothing.

310
00:27:12,799 --> 00:27:16,017
So, they will share their meal so everyone will have half a meal.

311
00:27:16,388 --> 00:27:19,819
Umar(عُمَر) said: Nobody will die if they're having half a meal,

312
00:27:20,784 --> 00:27:24,978
that was his plan if this would have extended but Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدالله) it didn't.

313
00:27:25,701 --> 00:27:27,560
The Muslims were making Dua(دُعَا),

314
00:27:27,584 --> 00:27:32,463
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said; I would see my father always repeating this Dua(دُعَا).

315
00:27:32,826 --> 00:27:35,588
اَللَّهُمُّ لَا تَجْعَلْ هَلَاكَ اُمَّتْ مُحَمَّدْاِلَى يَدِي

316
00:27:36,062 --> 00:27:42,216
O Allah don't make the Ummah(امة) of Muhammad(محمد) parish on my hands, under my authority

317
00:27:42,755 --> 00:27:46,109
I'm the one who is governing now,

318
00:27:46,391 --> 00:27:51,827
I'm the one responsible for their affairs. Don't let them die in this time.

319
00:27:51,867 --> 00:27:54,730
Don't let the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ die under my hands

320
00:27:56,609 --> 00:28:03,236
and that is when, Umar Bin Khattabرضي الله عنه took Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(ألعباس بن عبدالمطلب) with him to Assalaat-Ul-Asqaa(الصلاة استسقاء).

321
00:28:04,546 --> 00:28:05,307
 And he said:

322
00:28:06,092 --> 00:28:10,753
اَللَّهُمَّ إِنَّا كُنَّانَتَوَسَّلُإلَيْكَ بِنَبِيِّنَا ﷺفَتَسْقِيْنَا,

323
00:28:11,941 --> 00:28:18,269
وَإِنَّانَتَوَسَّلُ إِلَيْكَ بِعَمِّ نَبِيِّنَا فَاسْقِنَا قَالَ :يَسْقَوْنَ

324
00:28:19,228 --> 00:28:20,661
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

325
00:28:21,844 --> 00:28:27,753
when Rasool Allah ﷺ was alive we used to make Waseela(وصيلة) through him that You (الله) give us rain.

326
00:28:28,186 --> 00:28:34,963
Now, since he passed away we asked You(الله) through his Uncle Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(ألعباس بن عبدالمطلب) to give us rain

327
00:28:35,205 --> 00:28:37,557
and Allah سبحانه تعالى sent down rain on them.

328
00:28:37,803 --> 00:28:39,359
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ).

329
00:28:47,778 --> 00:28:53,212
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) stopped the application of the punishment of stealing.

330
00:28:54,083 --> 00:28:57,581
So, no hands were amputated during that year.

331
00:28:59,101 --> 00:29:05,144
Some people say that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) what he has done,

332
00:29:05,773 --> 00:29:08,784
is he stopped applying the Hadd(حدّ).

333
00:29:09,570 --> 00:29:11,681
It wasn't really that he stopped applying it.

334
00:29:11,946 --> 00:29:16,528
What happened was, there was never a case, where it qualified for punishment

335
00:29:18,325 --> 00:29:22,898
because Rasool Allah ﷺ says, and this Hadith(حديث) is in Musnad Abdur-Razzaq(مسند عبدالرزاق)

336
00:29:23,981 --> 00:29:28,381
لَا يُقْطَعْ فِيْ الُعِذْقِ , وَلَا عَامْ اَلسَّنَةْ

337
00:29:29,882 --> 00:29:34,420
You do not amputate when there is famine,

338
00:29:36,093 --> 00:29:40,798
You do not apply the Hadd(حدّ) of As-Sarqah(السرقة), of stealing when there is famine.

339
00:29:41,396 --> 00:29:47,233
If people are stealing to live their hand are not amputated.

340
00:29:48,575 --> 00:29:54,774
The hands of burglar is amputated when they can live, but they are still stealing.

341
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:59,488
But if somebody is, stealing for the sole purpose of just surviving,

342
00:30:00,687 --> 00:30:03,418
then in this situation, even though it is Haram(حرام),

343
00:30:03,766 --> 00:30:06,676
but the Hadd(حدّ) of amputation is not applied.

344
00:30:07,176 --> 00:30:10,719
And that is what happened during the time Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

345
00:30:14,762 --> 00:30:17,194
An important lesson to learn from this.

346
00:30:17,964 --> 00:30:33,412
You know, sometimes we get to carried away and we say that you know, if we would just apply Sharia(شريعة),

347
00:30:35,348 --> 00:30:38,622
Allah would flood us with blessings and we would all become rich

348
00:30:38,654 --> 00:30:43,186
and we would all own brand new Mercedes Benz or BMW's.

349
00:30:43,211 --> 00:30:44,857
We would have these huge mansions.

350
00:30:45,224 --> 00:30:49,391
All what we have to do is apply Shariah(شرية) and we're all going to become rich and wealthy,

351
00:30:54,950 --> 00:30:57,081
and sometimes such promises are made.

352
00:30:57,152 --> 00:31:06,726
You know sometimes when you have elections in some Muslim countries and the Islamists would say,

353
00:31:07,406 --> 00:31:12,051
we will solve economical problems, we'll take care of your needs, we will do this and that?

354
00:31:14,783 --> 00:31:16,834
Is that something that Rasool Allah ﷺ did

355
00:31:17,096 --> 00:31:20,657
or is it something that the Sahabahرضى الله عنهم promised their followers.

356
00:31:20,872 --> 00:31:23,996
Did they say just become Muslim in your pocket will be loaded ?

357
00:31:27,497 --> 00:31:38,651
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was discussing the terms of Bay'ah Ul-Aqabah(بيعةالعقبه) the Pledge of Allegiance with Al-Ansaar(الانصار),

358
00:31:39,500 --> 00:31:48,605
 this is one of the most important treaties or agreements that Rasool Allah ﷺ was involved in.

359
00:31:51,001 --> 00:31:57,196
Rasool Allah ﷺ was asking the Ansaar(أنْصَار) to commit their lives and their wealth

360
00:31:57,503 --> 00:31:59,001
that's not a very easy commitment.

361
00:31:59,903 --> 00:32:02,294
It's not easy to go to some people and tell them,

362
00:32:02,918 --> 00:32:06,706
I want you to put your life and wealth on the line.

363
00:32:08,537 --> 00:32:11,611
It's impossible, to ask somebody to do that.

364
00:32:12,208 --> 00:32:17,176
That's what Rasool Allah ﷺ was asking the Ansaar(أنْصَار), he was telling them.

365
00:32:17,207 --> 00:32:21,876
I want you to protect me just like you protect your wives and your children.

366
00:32:22,303 --> 00:32:24,189
Do you agree? They said: Yes! We are agree.

367
00:32:24,335 --> 00:32:25,964
One of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار)  stood up and said, listen

368
00:32:25,988 --> 00:32:28,214
you understand the implications of this agreement.

369
00:32:29,297 --> 00:32:33,365
This means that the Arabs and non Arabs are going to come against you,

370
00:32:35,344 --> 00:32:38,665
this is not something to be taken lightly.

371
00:32:39,329 --> 00:32:49,448
And then he said: You either promise him and fulfill that promise or pull out of it now, before it's too late.

372
00:32:50,918 --> 00:32:56,043
You don't have to commit there's no agreement yet, we didn't give our word yet.

373
00:32:56,550 --> 00:32:58,982
So, pull out of it now, this is the Al-Habbab Al-Mundhir(الحبَّاب المنذر),

374
00:32:59,963 --> 00:33:05,610
and Al-Abbas(العباس) had some similar words, he said Muhammad(محمد) is protected among his people

375
00:33:05,657 --> 00:33:07,707
 and you are the one inviting him to your land.

376
00:33:07,963 --> 00:33:09,835
Are you sure that you're able to protect him?

377
00:33:11,301 --> 00:33:14,473
So, all warnings were given to Al-Ansaar(الانصار) afore time.

378
00:33:14,778 --> 00:33:17,258
They knew it very well, Al-Habbab Al-Mundhir(الحبَّاب المنذر), told them that,

379
00:33:17,426 --> 00:33:19,346
 Al Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(ألعباس بن عبدالمطلب) told them that,

380
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:21,251
you are getting your hands in hot water.

381
00:33:24,398 --> 00:33:25,731
What did Al-Ansaar(الانصار) say?

382
00:33:26,499 --> 00:33:29,096
They said: All right that's our part of the bargain.

383
00:33:29,691 --> 00:33:31,509
What will we get?

384
00:33:32,826 --> 00:33:34,656
What is our part?

385
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:40,615
You see, our commitment to this agreement is, we put our lives and wealth on the line.

386
00:33:40,806 --> 00:33:42,735
What will you give us in exchange?

387
00:33:44,658 --> 00:33:50,242
 Did Rasool Allah ﷺ tell them I promise you five ministries in the government?

388
00:33:51,025 --> 00:33:55,247
 Did he tell them I will promise you this number of seats in the parliament?

389
00:33:55,903 --> 00:33:58,984
Did he tell them that I promise you half of the wealth?

390
00:33:59,559 --> 00:34:01,921
Did he tell them I will make you kings after me?

391
00:34:02,796 --> 00:34:11,804
Like for example with Rabiyyah(ربيعة), when Rasool Allah ﷺ was discussing with them,

392
00:34:11,829 --> 00:34:17,069
because Rasool Allah ﷺ went to meet many different tribes and they all turned him down,

393
00:34:17,984 --> 00:34:25,832
but this tribe from Iraq, they said: This man if we take him with us

394
00:34:26,638 --> 00:34:29,114
we can eat with him, the Arabs and the non Arabs.

395
00:34:29,216 --> 00:34:32,151
They saw some abilities in Muhammadﷺ. They said: We could use him

396
00:34:33,369 --> 00:34:34,490
we could use him for our benefit.

397
00:34:35,977 --> 00:34:38,877
So, when they were discussing with Muhammadﷺ.

398
00:34:40,244 --> 00:34:44,846
Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه told them: What he expects from them. They said;

399
00:34:45,545 --> 00:34:49,935
We agree as long as you give us the kingdom after you.

400
00:34:51,295 --> 00:34:54,640
As long as you transfer power to us, after you pass away.

401
00:34:55,391 --> 00:34:57,069
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say:? He said;

402
00:34:57,147 --> 00:35:08,024
اِنَّا الْاَرْضَ لله يُوْرِثُهَا مَنْ يَشَاءُ وَلْعَاقِبَةُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ۝

403
00:35:08,493 --> 00:35:14,142
This earth belongs to Allah and Allah will give it to whomever He wills,

404
00:35:14,544 --> 00:35:16,729
 and the end belongs to the pious.

405
00:35:17,599 --> 00:35:21,267
In the end, the victorious will be the Muttaqeen(متقين).

406
00:35:21,685 --> 00:35:24,537
But Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying: This is something, I cannot commit to.

407
00:35:24,795 --> 00:35:28,690
This is something in the hands of Allah, I cannot promise you kingdom and power.

408
00:35:29,210 --> 00:35:31,844
This is something that belongs to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, I don't have that authority.

409
00:35:33,311 --> 00:35:35,275
So, the Al-Ansaar(الانصار) are saying, what are you going to give us?

410
00:35:35,347 --> 00:35:36,609
because it's an agreement.

411
00:35:37,790 --> 00:35:41,579
there's a transaction, exchange.

412
00:35:42,415 --> 00:35:44,670
We are going to give our lives and our wealth.

413
00:35:44,782 --> 00:35:46,306
What are we going to get back.?

414
00:35:47,132 --> 00:35:48,587
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say:?

415
00:35:49,325 --> 00:35:53,829
One word, Al-Jannah(الجنة)! Paradise.

416
00:35:54,548 --> 00:35:56,812
That’s all what can I offer you.

417
00:35:57,817 --> 00:35:58,849
What did they say?

418
00:35:59,073 --> 00:36:02,640
قَالُوْ رَبَيْهَ الْبَيْعَ لَا نَقِيْلُوْ وَلَا نَسْتَقِيْلَ

419
00:36:03,019 --> 00:36:07,324
They said: What a profitable trade, we will never give up.

420
00:36:09,490 --> 00:36:10,830
What is better than Jannah(جنة).

421
00:36:12,404 --> 00:36:14,420
They said: This is the best deal we could ask for.

422
00:36:15,787 --> 00:36:16,988
لا نقيلو ولا نستقيل

423
00:36:17,012 --> 00:36:19,805
You will never find us backing out of it.

424
00:36:20,267 --> 00:36:24,267
We will be there and they were true to their word.

425
00:36:24,953 --> 00:36:27,543
Al-Ansaar(الانصار) they fought until the last moment

426
00:36:28,277 --> 00:36:31,719
they gave their lives to Rasool Allah ﷺ, everything.

427
00:36:36,387 --> 00:36:39,480
So, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tests you in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

428
00:36:39,561 --> 00:36:43,602
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) one of the greatest of Al-Khulafah(ألخلفاء)

429
00:36:46,500 --> 00:36:49,200
but still a famine occurred during his reign,

430
00:36:50,602 --> 00:36:52,547
people were dying due to hunger.

431
00:36:54,257 --> 00:36:56,154
So, you cannot really promise people Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

432
00:36:56,278 --> 00:36:57,899
You I cannot tell them that I'm going to offer you Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

433
00:36:57,924 --> 00:37:00,532
That's not something in your hands.

434
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:05,763
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and the Muslims were tested. He said:

435
00:37:06,141 --> 00:37:08,005
إِبْتُلِيْتُمْ بِيْ وَ أُبْتَلِيْتُ بِكُمْ

436
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:12,077
He said: I am tested through you and you're tested through me.

437
00:37:15,751 --> 00:37:19,388
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه was worried maybe this is because of my sins,

438
00:37:19,413 --> 00:37:20,641
Maybe it's because of your sins.

439
00:37:20,681 --> 00:37:25,257
He said: This is happening to us either because of my sins or your sins or the sins of all of us.

440
00:37:26,560 --> 00:37:29,294
So, make Tauba(توبة) and ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to forgive you

441
00:37:30,518 --> 00:37:35,291
and that would be his Dua(دُعَا) in Assalaat-Ul-Asqaa(الصلاة استسقاء)

442
00:37:35,517 --> 00:37:38,412
and in the Khutub(خطب) that he would give, he would keep on saying:

443
00:37:38,436 --> 00:37:42,908
اَسْتَغْفِرُاللهَ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهَ، اَسْتَغْفِرُاللهَ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهَ، اَسْتَغْفِرُاللهَ وَ اَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهَ،

444
00:37:43,726 --> 00:37:47,780
Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says in Qur'an in Sur'at Nooh(سورة نوح),

445
00:37:48,632 --> 00:37:53,609
اِسْتَغْفِرُوا رَبّكُمْ إِنَّهُ كَانَ غَفَّارًا ۝ يُرْسِل السَّمَاء عَلَيْكُمْ مِدْرَارًا۝

446
00:37:54,816 --> 00:37:58,999
وَيُمْدِدْكُمْ بِأَمْوَالٍ وَبَنِينَ وَيَجْعَلْ لَكُمْ جَنَّاتٍ وَيَجْعَلْ لَكُمْ أَنْهَارًا۝

447
00:37:59,511 --> 00:38:04,775
Ask Allah  forgiveness, Allah is forgiving, He would send down rain on you from the sky.

448
00:38:06,217 --> 00:38:09,101
So, forgiveness in Assalaat-Ul-Asqaa(الصلاة استسقاء) you make Istaghfar(أستغفار).

449
00:38:10,037 --> 00:38:11,504
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very sensitive.

450
00:38:11,529 --> 00:38:16,840
He would see that natural occurrences are influenced by your actions.

451
00:38:17,742 --> 00:38:21,911
So, when there was an earthquake in Madina during the reign of Umar(عُمَر)

452
00:38:24,805 --> 00:38:26,864
and then the earthquake happened again.

453
00:38:26,888 --> 00:38:29,558
He stood on the pulpit and he gathered the Muslims and he said;

454
00:38:30,406 --> 00:38:37,141
"This earthquake is because of your sins and if this earthquake happens a third time, I'm going to leave you.

455
00:38:37,543 --> 00:38:40,399
" I'm leaving, I'm getting, I'm walking out of Madina.

456
00:38:41,059 --> 00:38:44,329
He said: You either stop these sins or I'm going to leave.

457
00:38:45,958 --> 00:38:49,641
So, he used to see that, this is because of what the people are doing.

458
00:38:51,208 --> 00:38:52,793
So, that could happen to the best.

459
00:38:52,910 --> 00:38:53,346
Why?

460
00:38:53,386 --> 00:38:55,249
Because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ purifies the best,

461
00:38:55,968 --> 00:39:00,628
you see with the Kafir(كافر), Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ rewards them for their good in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

462
00:39:01,350 --> 00:39:03,974
So, that they will meet him on the Day of Judgment without any good deeds.

463
00:39:05,228 --> 00:39:09,775
And the believer Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ punishes him in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) for his sins.

464
00:39:10,189 --> 00:39:13,365
So, that he meets Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on the Day of Judgment without any sins.

465
00:39:14,858 --> 00:39:21,848
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: If loves the person he would test him through trials and tribulations in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

466
00:39:22,123 --> 00:39:26,707
So, that he would be walking on the face of the earth without any sins, cleansed.

467
00:39:28,367 --> 00:39:33,117
So, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ was testing Umar(عُمَر) and Allah was testing the Muslims and they were dying, famine.

468
00:39:37,003 --> 00:39:43,328
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the same year another crisis or catastrophe occurred in Ash-Sham(ألشام)

469
00:39:44,136 --> 00:39:51,580
in the 18 year of Hijrah(هجرة) and that was the plague of Umwaas(عمواس), Ta'oon Amwaas(طاعون عمواس)

470
00:39:51,992 --> 00:39:55,707
Amwaas(عمواس), is a town next to Jerusalem.

471
00:39:59,070 --> 00:40:05,617
Amwaas(عمواس) is a village close to Jerusalem Al-Qudus(القدس)

472
00:40:06,539 --> 00:40:13,635
and that's where the plague started and it just spread out all over Ash-sham(ألشام)

473
00:40:16,838 --> 00:40:24,644
claiming the lives of the population of Ash-sham(ألشام) many of the Muslims died.

474
00:40:28,537 --> 00:40:33,001
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was on his way to Ash-sham(ألشام) and they told him, that there's a plague

475
00:40:35,930 --> 00:40:39,707
 and they told him, don't go to Ash-sham(ألشام).

476
00:40:41,868 --> 00:40:46,821
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) made Shuraa(شورى), consultation with the Sahabah(صحابه),

477
00:40:47,540 --> 00:40:49,895
some of them said: You go, some said, you don't.

478
00:40:51,032 --> 00:40:55,067
For example Muslima Al-Fath(مسلمة الفتح), the late Muslims they all said: Don't go.

479
00:40:55,957 --> 00:40:59,938
Some of the early Muslims they said: This is the Qadar( القدر) of Allah, just go.

480
00:41:01,410 --> 00:41:03,271
Abdur Rahman Bin Auf( عبدالرحمن بن عوف) came and said;

481
00:41:03,615 --> 00:41:07,122
I have a Hadith(حديث) from Rasool Allah ﷺ, regarding that.

482
00:41:08,074 --> 00:41:10,066
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

483
00:41:10,552 --> 00:41:14,519
إِذَا سَمِعْتُمْ بِهَذَا الْوَبَاءْ بِبَلَدٍ(بِطَّاعُوْنِ فِيْ الاَرْضٍ) فَلَا تَقْدِمُوْا عَلَيْهِ

484
00:41:14,782 --> 00:41:18,613
وَإِذَا وَقَعَ(بِاالاَرْضٍ) بِبَلَدٍوَأَنْتُمْ فِيْهِ فَلَا تَخْرِجُوْافِرَارًا مِّنْه

485
00:41:19,118 --> 00:41:21,894
And this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim(ألمسلم), Abdur Rahman Bin Auf(عبدالرحمن بن عوف) said;

486
00:41:22,094 --> 00:41:26,061
If you hear about the plague in a town… do not enter it,

487
00:41:26,667 --> 00:41:28,934
and if you are already there… Do not leave.

488
00:41:31,347 --> 00:41:34,940
So, if you're outside don't go inside, if you're inside do not leave

489
00:41:35,839 --> 00:41:40,420
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), this is the modern day, quarantine

490
00:41:40,531 --> 00:41:42,731
 you do not allow anything to come from outside

491
00:41:43,239 --> 00:41:46,212
and in the same time, you don't allow the people who are infected from leaving.

492
00:41:47,411 --> 00:41:52,291
So, this is the proper health regulation nothing comes in and nothing goes out.

493
00:41:53,695 --> 00:41:56,628
So, when there is a Hadith(حديث) from Rasool Allah ﷺ, the Sahabah(صحابه) agreed

494
00:41:56,851 --> 00:41:59,731
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went back to Madina.

495
00:42:02,817 --> 00:42:05,660
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه sent a letter to Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة).

496
00:42:05,685 --> 00:42:07,141
Umar(عُمَر) used to love Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة).

497
00:42:08,030 --> 00:42:09,278
 He used to love him so much.

498
00:42:09,543 --> 00:42:11,424
So, he sends him a letter, he said;

499
00:42:12,475 --> 00:42:18,784
سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكَ,أَمَّا بَعْدَ، فَإِنَّه’ قَدْ عَرَضَتْ لِيْ حَاجَةْ أُشَافِهَكْ فِيْهَا

500
00:42:19,569 --> 00:42:25,468
فَعَزَمْتُ عَلَيْكَ إِذَا نَظَرْتَ فِيْ كِتَابِيْ هَذَا أَلَّاتَضَعْه’ مِنْ يَدِكَ حَتَّى تُقْبِلَ إِلَيً,

501
00:42:26,152 --> 00:42:31,063
He said: I have something that I want to talk to you about and

502
00:42:31,441 --> 00:42:33,785
I have to do it verbally face to face.

503
00:42:34,789 --> 00:42:39,771
So, when you receive this letter from me, do not drop it, until you come here.

504
00:42:42,305 --> 00:42:45,444
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) understood, what Umar(عُمَر) meant by that.

505
00:42:46,854 --> 00:42:49,348
Umar(عُمَر) was trying to pull Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) out.

506
00:42:54,260 --> 00:42:59,528
Abu Obaidah رضي الله عنه, because he wasn't affected yet

507
00:42:59,553 --> 00:43:01,927
and maybe the plague didn't reach that area yet.

508
00:43:03,809 --> 00:43:05,560
So, Umar(عُمَر) wanted him to come out.

509
00:43:07,981 --> 00:43:11,437
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) sent him a letter back. He said;

510
00:43:13,307 --> 00:43:22,271
يَا اَمِيْرُ الْمُو مِنِيْنَ إِنِّيْ قَدْ عَرَفْتُ حَاجَتَكَ إِلَيّْ وَإِنِّيْ فِيْ جُنْدٍ مِّنَّ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ لَا أَجِدُبِنَفْسِيْ رَغْبَةً عَنْهُمْ

511
00:43:22,807 --> 00:43:29,325
فَلَسْتُ أُرِيْدُ فِرَاقَهُمْ حَتَّى يَقْضِيْ اللهُ فِيْيَ وَفِيْهِمْ أَمْرَه’ وَقَضَاهْ ,

512
00:43:29,744 --> 00:43:33,397
فَحَلِّلْنِيْ مِنْ عَزْمَتِكَ يا أمير المومنين وَدَعْنِيْ فِيْ جُنْدِيْ

513
00:43:34,050 --> 00:43:37,896
He said:, O, Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), I know, why you want me to come.

514
00:43:39,146 --> 00:43:41,465
I know why you want me to come.

515
00:43:42,521 --> 00:43:44,481
But I'm among my soldiers,

516
00:43:45,767 --> 00:43:47,408
I'm among my soldiers.

517
00:43:48,367 --> 00:43:52,261
And I don't want to give myself preference over them.

518
00:43:53,086 --> 00:43:55,580
What is going to happen to them is going to happen to me

519
00:43:56,303 --> 00:44:00,748
and I'm going to stay with them until, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ brings down his Qadha'a(قضاء),

520
00:44:00,787 --> 00:44:01,957
brings down his judgment.

521
00:44:02,959 --> 00:44:05,387
So, please, Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) excuse me,

522
00:44:05,811 --> 00:44:07,263
 and allow me to stay behind.

523
00:44:08,720 --> 00:44:11,472
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) did not want to desert his soldiers,

524
00:44:11,866 --> 00:44:14,902
you either call us all back or I'm going to stay with them.

525
00:44:15,772 --> 00:44:17,105
If they die, we die together.

526
00:44:18,669 --> 00:44:20,135
But I'm not going to leave my soldiers.

527
00:44:21,670 --> 00:44:27,270
So, Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) because of his loyalty towards his soldiers, he lost his life.

