00:47:30,177 --> 00:47:33,531
That's the only reason why I want to be in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), not to gather wealth

569
00:47:34,809 --> 00:47:36,639
it is to get closer to You, O Allah.

570
00:47:37,308 --> 00:47:41,006
And if this is the time for me to meet you, I welcomed that appointment.

571
00:47:54,240 --> 00:47:59,659
THE FINANCIAL SITUATION OF THE KHILAFAH(خِلَافَه).

572
00:48:02,756 --> 00:48:04,089
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

573
00:48:04,776 --> 00:48:13,338
وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّمَا غَنِمْتُمْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ فَأَنَّ لِلَّهِ خُمُسَهُ وَلِلرَّسُولِ وَلِذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ

574
00:48:13,783 --> 00:48:21,846
 إِنْ كُنْتُمْ آمَنْتُمْ بِاللَّهِ وَمَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَىٰ عَبْدِنَا يَوْمَ الْفُرْقَانِ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ۝

575
00:48:21,870 --> 00:48:24,649
Al-Anfal(ألأنفال) Verse 41, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

576
00:48:25,133 --> 00:48:29,933
"And know that out of all the booty that you may acquire, in war,

577
00:48:30,123 --> 00:48:32,511
a fifth share is assigned to Allah,

578
00:48:32,824 --> 00:48:37,996
and to the messenger and to the near relatives, orphans, the needy, and the wayfarer,

579
00:48:38,744 --> 00:48:41,601
if you do believe in Allah, and in the revelation

580
00:48:41,834 --> 00:48:44,558
we sent down to our servant on the day of testing

581
00:48:44,726 --> 00:48:49,000
the day of the meeting of the two forces for Allah has power over all things."

582
00:48:49,347 --> 00:48:54,000
This Ayah(آية) reveals the Hukum(حكم), the ruling on Ghanimah(غنيمه),

583
00:48:54,024 --> 00:48:55,984
Ghanimah(غنيمه) is the spoils of war.

584
00:48:56,636 --> 00:48:59,736
It states that one fifth of the spoils of war

585
00:49:01,110 --> 00:49:11,567
goes to Allah, Rasool Allah ﷺ, the Miskeen(مسكين), Ibn Sabeel(إبن سبيل), and the Yateem(يتيم).

586
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:17,499
The other four fifths go to the fighters.

587
00:49:17,806 --> 00:49:25,110
So, for example, if you had, let's say 100 pounds, 80 pounds would go to the fighters

588
00:49:26,108 --> 00:49:28,948
and then those 80 pounds are going to be split among the fighters.

589
00:49:29,034 --> 00:49:33,830
The horseman gets one share for himself and two shares for his horse

590
00:49:34,234 --> 00:49:36,634
and the foot soldier gets one share.

591
00:49:38,273 --> 00:49:42,460
The 20% or the 20 pounds that is going to Allah,

592
00:49:43,273 --> 00:49:49,334
Rasool Ullah, the Yateem(يتيم) the Ibn Sabeel(إبن سبيل) and Al-Miskeen(مسكين)

593
00:49:49,635 --> 00:49:54,926
is split into five, so 20% by five is 4%.

594
00:49:55,497 --> 00:49:59,205
So, 4% goes to Allah, 4% goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ

595
00:49:59,517 --> 00:50:04,338
4% to the Yateem(يتيم), four% to the orphan I mean Yateem(يتيم)

596
00:50:04,363 --> 00:50:08,983
and 4% goes to the poor and 4% Ibn Sabeel(إبن سبيل), the wayfarer.

597
00:50:09,876 --> 00:50:12,352
That's the ruling on Ghanimah(غنيمه).

598
00:50:13,355 --> 00:50:14,885
Now, when we say it goes to Allah

599
00:50:14,909 --> 00:50:22,945
Rasool Allah ﷺ spends his 4% and the 4% that goes to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, as he deems fit.

600
00:50:23,794 --> 00:50:25,584
So, it is Rasool Allah ﷺ who spends it

601
00:50:25,852 --> 00:50:26,953
في مصالحل المسلمين

602
00:50:27,191 --> 00:50:28,682
what benefits the Muslims.

603
00:50:29,568 --> 00:50:32,202
Ghanimah(غنيمه) there's something called Ghanimah(غنيمه) and there is Fae(فيئ).

604
00:50:32,325 --> 00:50:35,380
Fae(فيئ) is what you take from the enemy without a fight.

605
00:50:35,652 --> 00:50:40,071
Ghanimah(غنيمه) is what is taken from the enemy through war.

606
00:50:41,009 --> 00:50:43,655
And this is an issue of Fiqh(فقه) that we're talking about because

607
00:50:44,168 --> 00:50:47,348
there was a discussion that occurred between Umar(عُمَر) and The Sahabah(صحابه)

608
00:50:47,372 --> 00:50:49,971
a very important discussion that occurred between them

609
00:50:50,228 --> 00:50:53,219
and it took a long time for them to sort it out.

610
00:50:54,715 --> 00:51:00,663
The ruling is that when there is a war and the Muslim army wins,

611
00:51:01,621 --> 00:51:06,444
they have the right to claim everything that they lay their hands on as their property

612
00:51:07,439 --> 00:51:08,510
including the people.

613
00:51:10,099 --> 00:51:15,144
So, the land, the money and the people become property for the Muslims

614
00:51:15,183 --> 00:51:18,656
 and that is then split, according to these rules.

615
00:51:19,541 --> 00:51:21,629
That is what Rasool Allah ﷺ did in Khaybar(خَيْبَر),

616
00:51:21,669 --> 00:51:23,597
that's what he did in the Ghazawaat(غزوات)

617
00:51:24,797 --> 00:51:27,230
that's the rule of Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

618
00:51:28,336 --> 00:51:40,578
Now, in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the Muslims opened vast, wealthy areas, Al Iraq, Ash-sham(ألشام) and Egypt.

619
00:51:41,533 --> 00:51:44,215
These were the jewels of the world in those days,

620
00:51:44,893 --> 00:51:50,180
the Roman and Persian Empire would fight over these lands because they are so lucrative.

621
00:51:51,379 --> 00:51:53,207
These are the fertile lands.

622
00:51:53,937 --> 00:51:58,262
Egypt because of the Nile, Al-Iraq because of the Euphrates River

623
00:51:58,515 --> 00:52:01,661
and then Ash-sham(ألشام) the Holy Land because of his religious significance

624
00:52:01,701 --> 00:52:05,493
but it's also blessed land is very fertile and blessed land very wealthy.

625
00:52:06,805 --> 00:52:09,340
So, the Roman Empire was in control of Egypt and Ash-sham(ألشام)

626
00:52:09,364 --> 00:52:11,112
and the Persian Empire was in control of Al-Iraq.

627
00:52:12,717 --> 00:52:15,117
When the Muslims opened these Lands,

628
00:52:15,914 --> 00:52:20,087
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) and Muad Ibn Jabal(معاذبن جبل) they came to  the Khalifah(خليفه) and they said;

629
00:52:20,928 --> 00:52:24,851
 If you gonna split up the land among the Muslims.

630
00:52:24,976 --> 00:52:28,059
So, you're splitting up the land and the people and everything among the Muslims.

631
00:52:29,001 --> 00:52:33,637
Muslims are going to own huge properties

632
00:52:35,130 --> 00:52:38,514
and then they're going to die and this will be inherited by their children

633
00:52:38,554 --> 00:52:42,006
and then inherited by the children of their children and it will go down the line

634
00:52:43,099 --> 00:52:46,272
and money will be accumulated within the hands of a few.

635
00:52:46,436 --> 00:52:51,282
I mean we were talking about huge pieces of land and these are very small armies.

636
00:52:51,764 --> 00:52:54,590
So, one soldier will end up owning towns.

637
00:52:56,103 --> 00:52:58,970
So, they said: You need to find a solution.

638
00:52:59,900 --> 00:53:04,396
Because after that how gonna we finance our Ghazawat(غزوات),

639
00:53:04,927 --> 00:53:10,185
if all of this money gets accumulated as private property, among the soldiers.

640
00:53:10,552 --> 00:53:12,372
How will you finance your campaigns?

641
00:53:12,435 --> 00:53:14,512
So, they were concerned about the continuation of Ghazuu(غزؤ).

642
00:53:15,484 --> 00:53:17,492
How will Ghazuu(غزؤ) carry on in the future

643
00:53:17,750 --> 00:53:20,887
if Iraq, Ash-sham(ألشام) and Egypt is split up among the soldiers.?

644
00:53:22,596 --> 00:53:27,418
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he considered these thoughts

645
00:53:28,300 --> 00:53:30,957
from Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذبن جبل) and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

646
00:53:31,113 --> 00:53:32,708
and it was becoming appealing to him.

647
00:53:34,616 --> 00:53:38,824
So, he called an assembly,

648
00:53:39,337 --> 00:53:42,345
the Sahabah(صحابه) came and he discussed the issue with them.

649
00:53:43,071 --> 00:53:46,104
Some of the Sahabah(صحابه) like Bilal(بلال) and Zubair(زبير), they said: No way.

650
00:53:47,150 --> 00:53:52,929
We're not going to allow somebody to take the property that we claimed through our own swords.

651
00:53:53,840 --> 00:53:59,037
No way will we give it to somebody who didn't attend this Ghazuu(غزؤ) with us,

652
00:54:00,432 --> 00:54:01,352
why should they get it.?

653
00:54:03,236 --> 00:54:06,111
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he saw resistance from some of the Sahabah(صحابه),

654
00:54:06,136 --> 00:54:09,494
he called in some of Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار),

655
00:54:09,686 --> 00:54:14,032
I actually read it to you the statements of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

656
00:54:14,124 --> 00:54:21,305
He started by reciting what he sees, what he views as the evidence to support his case.

657
00:54:21,791 --> 00:54:23,537
And these are the Ayaat(آيات) from Surat Al-Hashar(سورة الحشر):

658
00:54:26,011 --> 00:54:30,081
"What Allah has bestowed on His messenger and taken away from them

659
00:54:30,527 --> 00:54:35,660
 for this he made no expedition with either cavalry or camelry.

660
00:54:35,684 --> 00:54:39,524
But Allah gives power to his messengers over any He pleases,

661
00:54:39,727 --> 00:54:41,426
and Allah has power over all things".

662
00:54:41,711 --> 00:54:45,329
So, Allah here is talking about the wealth, that's taken from the enemies of Allah

663
00:54:45,533 --> 00:54:47,123
and put in the hands of Rasool Ullah.

664
00:54:47,298 --> 00:54:48,755
How was that split?

665
00:54:50,447 --> 00:54:56,442
it says: This is from verse six to 10, let me read them.

666
00:54:56,467 --> 00:55:00,831
"What Allah has bestowed on His messenger, and taken away from the people of the townships

667
00:55:01,171 --> 00:55:05,138
belongs to Allah to His Messenger, and to the kindred and orphans,

668
00:55:05,416 --> 00:55:11,769
the needy, and the wayfarer, in order that it may not merely make a circuit between the wealthy among you.

669
00:55:12,300 --> 00:55:14,516
So, take what the messenger assigns to you,

670
00:55:14,802 --> 00:55:20,511
and deny yourself that which He withhold from you and fear Allah, for Allah is strict in punishment.

671
00:55:21,845 --> 00:55:26,304
Some part is due to the indigent Mohajer(مهاجر)'s

672
00:55:26,654 --> 00:55:29,640
those who were expelled from their homes and their property

673
00:55:30,045 --> 00:55:32,436
while seeking grace from Allah and His good pleasure

674
00:55:32,823 --> 00:55:36,681
and aiding Allah and His Messenger such are indeed the sincere ones.

675
00:55:37,049 --> 00:55:39,108
So the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) have a claim to fae(فيئ),

676
00:55:40,034 --> 00:55:44,589
but those who before them, had homes in Madina, and had adopted the faith

677
00:55:44,923 --> 00:55:48,147
show their affection to such as came to them for refuge

678
00:55:48,536 --> 00:55:53,107
and entertain no desire in their hearts for things given to the latter,

679
00:55:53,491 --> 00:55:55,900
but give them preference over themselves,

680
00:55:56,186 --> 00:56:05,710
even though poverty was their own lot, and those saved from the covetousness of their souls.

681
00:56:06,033 --> 00:56:08,242
They are the ones that achieve prosperity."

682
00:56:08,282 --> 00:56:09,815
This is talking about Al-Ansaar(الانصار),

683
00:56:11,064 --> 00:56:14,385
And those who came after them, and say: Our Lord, forgive us

684
00:56:14,791 --> 00:56:18,174
and our brethren who came before us into the faith,

685
00:56:18,475 --> 00:56:24,700
and leave not in our hearts, rancor or sense of injury against those who have believed.

686
00:56:24,897 --> 00:56:28,531
Our Lord, You are indeed full of kindness most merciful.

687
00:56:29,989 --> 00:56:32,598
To summarize what these Ayaat(آيات) are saying regarding the fae(فيئ),

688
00:56:32,980 --> 00:56:37,149
it goes to the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), the Ansaar(أنْصَار) and the ones who come after them.

689
00:56:37,173 --> 00:56:41,286
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying that the ones who come after you have a claim to the fae(فيئ).

690
00:56:48,697 --> 00:56:49,982
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

691
00:56:50,501 --> 00:56:57,128
وَاللهِ لَا يُفْتَحْ بَعْدِيْ بَلَدْ فَيَكُوْنُ فِيْهِ كَبِيْرَ نَيْلٍ بَلْ عَسَى أَنْ يَكُوْنَ كَلَّا عَلَى الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ،

692
00:56:57,908 --> 00:57:06,367
فَإِذَا قَسَّمْتُ أَرْضَ الْعِرَاقِ بِعَلُوْجِهَا, وَأَرْضُ الشَّامِ بِعَلُوْجِهَا, فَمَايَسَدُّ بِهِ الثُّغُورْ؟

693
00:57:06,871 --> 00:57:07,823
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

694
00:57:08,220 --> 00:57:12,966
I don't think that any land we're going to open after this, will be as wealthy as this land.

695
00:57:13,220 --> 00:57:17,605
 In fact, the land that we may open in the future will be a liability for us,

696
00:57:18,684 --> 00:57:21,419
 it will be a burden on us,

697
00:57:21,622 --> 00:57:25,857
we will open it for Da'wah(دعوة) but in terms of the wealth it will be a burden on us

698
00:57:26,333 --> 00:57:27,810
because these are the richest lands.

699
00:57:29,331 --> 00:57:31,311
So, if I split Al-Iraq, and it's Ulooj(علوج).

