00:57:40,951 --> 00:57:44,208
How will we finance our camps, the military camps.

703
00:57:44,732 --> 00:57:49,619
وَمَا يَكُوْنُ للِذُّرِّيَّةْ وَالْأَرَامِلْ لِهَذَا الْبَلَدْ وَبِغَيْرِهِ مِنْ أَرَاضِي الشَّامِ وَالْعِرَاقْ؟

704
00:57:49,881 --> 00:57:54,514
And how will the orphans and widows live in this land and in Iraq and Ash-sham(ألشام),

705
00:57:54,862 --> 00:57:56,623
if all of the land is already split up.

706
00:57:58,205 --> 00:57:59,232
فَأَكْثَرُا عَلَى عمر

707
00:57:59,681 --> 00:58:01,865
So, they resisted that idea fiercely.

708
00:58:02,841 --> 00:58:03,592
They said;

709
00:58:03,649 --> 00:58:08,372
تَقِفْ مَا أَفَاءْ اَللهُ عَلَيْنَا بِأَسْيَافِنَا عَلَى قَوْمِ لَّمْ يَحْضُرُوْا وَلَمْ يَشْهَدُوْا,

710
00:58:08,900 --> 00:58:11,444
وَلأَبْنَاءِ الْقَوْمْ وَأَبْنَائِهِمْ وَلَمْ يَحْضَرُوْا

711
00:58:11,613 --> 00:58:14,797
You want to give the land that we opened with our own swords

712
00:58:15,035 --> 00:58:17,375
to people who did not witness this opening.

713
00:58:18,414 --> 00:58:21,909
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: This is but an opinion.

714
00:58:22,830 --> 00:58:24,360
This is just an opinion.

715
00:58:25,148 --> 00:58:28,668
And then they said: Well then you seek counsel.

716
00:58:29,057 --> 00:58:35,028
So, he invited 10 of the leaders of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار), Al Aos wal- Khazraj(ألأوس ولخزرج)  and he said;

717
00:58:37,040 --> 00:58:45,336
I'm one of you and you can see that some accepted my suggestion while some rejected it

718
00:58:46,317 --> 00:58:50,972
and I don't want you to follow me just because I like this idea.

719
00:58:51,820 --> 00:58:54,178
I want you to follow it because you believe it’s the truth.

720
00:58:55,539 --> 00:59:01,528
He said: Tell me what is your opinion. He said;

721
00:59:02,441 --> 00:59:09,186
وَلَكِنْ رَّأَيْتُ أَنَّه’ لَمْ يَبْقَ شَيْء يُفْتَحْ بَعْدَ أَرْضَ كِسْرَى وَقَدْ غَنِمْنَا الله أَمْوَالَهُمْ وَأَرْضَهُمْ وَعَلُوْجَهُمْ

722
00:59:09,807 --> 00:59:12,054
فَقَسَّمْتُ مَا غَنَمُوْا وَمِنْ أَمْوَالِهِمْ بَيْنَ أَهْلِهْ

723
00:59:12,253 --> 00:59:16,552
He said: The land of Kisra(كسرى), I have taken all of the wealth and I already split among you.

724
00:59:16,576 --> 00:59:20,304
So, the wealth was split among them it was just the land and the people.

725
00:59:20,689 --> 00:59:24,710
The people were not enslaved and the land was still in their hands.

726
00:59:27,634 --> 00:59:27,853
He said;

727
00:59:27,877 --> 00:59:34,704
وَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ أَنْ أَحْبِسَ الْأَرْضِيْنَ بِعَلُوْجِهَا وَاضِعًا عَلَيْهِمْ فِيْهَا الْخِرَاجْ وَفِيْ رِقَابِهِمِ الْجِزْيَةْ

728
00:59:34,729 --> 00:59:41,092
My suggestion is that all of this land becomes public property owned by the government

729
00:59:41,698 --> 00:59:48,509
and the owners, the former owners, the disbelievers who owned that land carry on working in it

730
00:59:49,247 --> 00:59:53,812
And they pay Al-Jizya(الجزية) and they pay a tax on the land, called Al-Kharaj(الخراج).

731
00:59:54,164 --> 00:59:58,455
So this was a new suggestion, but they pay a tax on the land.

732
01:00:00,391 --> 01:00:04,365
أَرَأَيْتُمْ هَذِهِ الثَغُوْرَ لَا بُدَّ لَهَا مِنْ رِجَالٍ يَلْزَمُوْنَهَا,

733
01:00:04,598 --> 01:00:09,258
أَرَأَيْتُمْ هَذِهِ الْمُدَنِ ألْعِظَامْ لَا بُدَّ لَهَا مِنْ أَنْ تُشْحِنَ بِالْجُيُوْشَ

734
01:00:10,849 --> 01:00:15,698
He said: Do you see all of these outposts they need to be filled with soldiers.

735
01:00:15,999 --> 01:00:19,334
Do you see all of these great towns, they need to be protected.

736
01:00:19,555 --> 01:00:20,598
Who's going to pay for this?

737
01:00:21,382 --> 01:00:24,702
So, the concern was how to spread the Da'wah(دعوة), how to carry on,

738
01:00:24,999 --> 01:00:26,748
with the Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

739
01:00:29,877 --> 01:00:33,223
They said the opinion is yours

740
01:00:33,747 --> 01:00:37,743
and if you don't do that, then the people of Kuffr(كفر) are going to come back to those towns.

741
01:00:39,374 --> 01:00:40,574
They said: We agree with you,

742
01:00:40,920 --> 01:00:47,090
 because if you don't, then there will be nobody to guard those towns

743
01:00:47,115 --> 01:00:48,475
and the kuffar will come back to them.

744
01:00:48,995 --> 01:00:52,663
So, this was the rise of the Muslim professional army.

745
01:00:53,745 --> 01:00:56,717
In the beginning in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ and in the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

746
01:00:57,519 --> 01:00:59,317
you didn't have professional soldiers.

747
01:00:59,888 --> 01:01:02,873
What you had, is the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, who are Civilians,

748
01:01:03,240 --> 01:01:08,021
they were the ones doing the fighting whenever the Imam(اِمَام) would give them the orders.

749
01:01:08,513 --> 01:01:12,450
But now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wants to appoint dedicated soldiers

750
01:01:12,787 --> 01:01:16,220
to the outpost and to guard the new Muslim towns

751
01:01:16,689 --> 01:01:22,533
and they need salaries and that's why you find that armies consume a lot of Money,

752
01:01:23,470 --> 01:01:27,962
they claim a major part of the budget of any nation

753
01:01:28,462 --> 01:01:33,640
and this burden was beginning to appear in the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

754
01:01:33,707 --> 01:01:37,787
when there was the nucleus of the professional army.

755
01:01:37,983 --> 01:01:41,479
So, he wanted to find money to finance that and this money would come from the land

756
01:01:41,897 --> 01:01:43,353
and from Al-Jizya(الجزية).

757
01:01:43,924 --> 01:01:46,075
So, that's where Kharaaj(خراج) came from.

758
01:01:46,399 --> 01:01:49,180
The first to apply the rule of Kharaaj(خراج) was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

759
01:01:49,205 --> 01:01:56,796
now again did he innovate in that or is this something that has its origins in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

760
01:01:57,677 --> 01:02:03,100
First of all he quoted the Ayaat(آيات) and he saw these Ayaat(آيات) as an evidence for him.

761
01:02:05,974 --> 01:02:13,562
 Now, you might say well Rasool Allah ﷺ he, divided the Ghanimah(غنيمة) among the fighters

762
01:02:13,976 --> 01:02:15,804
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not do that.

763
01:02:16,002 --> 01:02:23,065
The answer would be that it is allowed to claim the land and the people and divided them among the soldiers

764
01:02:23,090 --> 01:02:24,788
but it's not mandatory to do so,

765
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:28,659
because Rasool Allah ﷺ did not do that when he opened Makkah.

766
01:02:29,804 --> 01:02:31,287
When Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Makkah,

767
01:02:31,312 --> 01:02:34,098
he did not claim the land and he did not enslaved the people.

768
01:02:35,702 --> 01:02:39,799
Therefore this is the evidence that it is an option and it's not mandatory to do that.

769
01:02:40,061 --> 01:02:44,185
Rasool Allah ﷺ set that people of Makkah free and he did not claim their land.

770
01:02:44,501 --> 01:02:46,666
So, no Ghanimah(غنيمه), was taken from Makkah.

771
01:02:46,884 --> 01:02:51,144
So, that's evidence to support Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) in what he has done,

772
01:02:51,382 --> 01:02:53,070
add to that the Shura(شورى),

773
01:02:53,582 --> 01:02:57,021
this was a decision that is reached through Shura(شورى).

774
01:02:59,527 --> 01:03:00,956
So, that's regarding Al-Kharaaj(ألخراج).

775
01:03:01,293 --> 01:03:08,246
And Al-Kharaj(ألخراج) was one of the greatest sources of income to the Muslim Treasury.

776
01:03:13,988 --> 01:03:21,875
And another new financial resource in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

777
01:03:25,874 --> 01:03:29,320
one of the Muslim leaders came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and said;

778
01:03:30,967 --> 01:03:37,795
The non Muslims are charging us, Customs - when we enter into their land to do business.

779
01:03:38,618 --> 01:03:40,007
Should we charge them.?

780
01:03:42,404 --> 01:03:46,896
They were charging customs on any Muslim businessmen,

781
01:03:46,932 --> 01:03:48,342
who are going into their lands.

782
01:03:49,291 --> 01:03:53,553
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: How much do they charge you? He said: 10%

783
01:03:53,822 --> 01:03:55,816
He said, well you charge them, 10%.

784
01:03:57,421 --> 01:04:02,377
So, this was the first time non Muslims were charged, when they enter into Muslim land to do business.

785
01:04:02,750 --> 01:04:06,125
That wasn't the case in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ or the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

786
01:04:07,316 --> 01:04:12,062
but Umar(عُمَر) wanted to treat them equally since they are charging our businessmen,

787
01:04:12,675 --> 01:04:15,925
to have a fair trade agreement we need to charge them too,

788
01:04:15,950 --> 01:04:17,967
otherwise we would be at a disadvantage.

789
01:04:18,601 --> 01:04:23,207
They come and do business in our land and they don't pay any customs while we paying 10%.

790
01:04:23,320 --> 01:04:25,215
 And this is called Al-Ushr(العشر).

791
01:04:26,524 --> 01:04:28,742
Al-Ushr(ألعشر) means one tenth.

792
01:04:29,506 --> 01:04:38,569
So, he started applying this charge on any non Muslims who would enter into the Muslim land to do business.

793
01:04:40,974 --> 01:04:45,474
Then you had Al-Ghanaem(ألغنائم), Al-Ghanaem(ألغنائم) were also a source of income.

794
01:04:45,590 --> 01:04:47,609
So, Al-Ghanimah(غنيمه) is the wealth that is taken,

795
01:04:48,043 --> 01:04:52,002
 and Al-Kharaj(ألخراج) is the money that is taken from the land, from the harvest.

796
01:04:52,949 --> 01:05:00,210
So Al-Kharaj(ألخراج) he would apply for example, out of a certain area of grape vines,

797
01:05:00,486 --> 01:05:05,498
you pay 10 Dirham(درهم), if it's dates you pay five Dirham(درهم) and so on

798
01:05:06,260 --> 01:05:09,064
Al-Ghanimah(غنيمه) is the wealth that is taken from the army

799
01:05:09,252 --> 01:05:11,515
and from the people that's called Ghanimah(غنيمه).

800
01:05:11,858 --> 01:05:17,323
And Ghanimah(غنيمه), when it came to KISRA(كسرى),

801
01:05:18,546 --> 01:05:24,761
The Romans and Persians in general, when they would go to fight they would go on with their wealth

802
01:05:25,221 --> 01:05:29,560
 for example, they would have gems, diamonds, gold,

803
01:05:30,049 --> 01:05:34,962
 their swords would have these treasures on them.

804
01:05:36,839 --> 01:05:42,507
So, a lot of that was claimed by the Muslim army, and the amounts were huge.

805
01:05:42,984 --> 01:05:49,759
For example, in the palace of Kisra(كسرى) they found this carpet or rug

806
01:05:52,053 --> 01:05:56,467
 it was three thousand six hundred 3600 Diraah(دراع) long.

807
01:05:57,737 --> 01:06:03,060
And Diraah(دراع) is something like a foot or even longer than a foot.

808
01:06:03,962 --> 01:06:05,542
So, we are talking about a huge rug.

809
01:06:06,415 --> 01:06:09,427
And the amazing thing about this rug is, it was three dimensions,

810
01:06:11,873 --> 01:06:21,320
it had statues in it and it had rivers flowing, it had animals and none of them were real.

811
01:06:23,242 --> 01:06:26,215
The water that was flowing or the rivers was gold.

812
01:06:28,071 --> 01:06:35,334
The animals were treasures, diamonds and gems, the mountains were silk.

813
01:06:36,388 --> 01:06:41,129
We are talking about the three dimension rug and it's packed with all of these valuables.

814
01:06:43,708 --> 01:06:47,785
They sold it and it fetched 20,000 Dirham(درهم)

815
01:06:49,708 --> 01:06:53,696
and they cut it into pieces, so Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) had a piece

816
01:06:53,778 --> 01:06:54,628
and other Sahabah(صحابه) has a piece.

817
01:06:54,668 --> 01:07:00,654
They weren't interested in keeping this huge rug as a souvenir or hanging it in Madina somewhere.

818
01:07:00,694 --> 01:07:02,390
They cut it into pieces and sold it.

819
01:07:05,609 --> 01:07:08,725
What's the use of having this, use it for Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

820
01:07:09,475 --> 01:07:14,344
For Example the Ghanimah(غنيمه) would be so much that at one point of time.

821
01:07:14,627 --> 01:07:19,405
The share of the soldier would be 15000 Dirham(درهم), which was huge amount of money.

822
01:07:21,845 --> 01:07:24,254
In Jaloolaah(جلولأء), the Ghanimah(غنيمه) was six Million.

823
01:07:27,394 --> 01:07:33,832
May be the effect of all of this wealth coming in, didn’t show up in the time of Umar(عُمَر) there is a lag.

824
01:07:35,022 --> 01:07:36,859
 But it showed up in the time of Uthman(عثمان).

825
01:07:37,554 --> 01:07:39,772
The Ghazawat(غزوات) happened in the time of Umar(عُمَر)

826
01:07:40,109 --> 01:07:45,107
but the fruits were showing in the time of Uthman رضي الله عنه.

827
01:07:45,616 --> 01:07:48,750
That’s when the Muslims were becoming very wealthy,

828
01:07:49,083 --> 01:07:52,849
and that’s when, when you had people like Abu Darda(ابودرداء) and Abu Dharr(ابو زر)

829
01:07:53,119 --> 01:07:55,953
 going around warning the Muslims from Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

830
01:07:57,166 --> 01:08:03,594
Abu Darda(ابودرداء) he would Stand in the square in Damascus and he would call the Muslims

831
01:08:03,920 --> 01:08:06,830
and saying: O people of Demashq(دمشق): Don’t you have Taqwa(تقوى).

832
01:08:07,677 --> 01:08:09,871
Don’t you see what happened to the people of Aad(عاد),

833
01:08:10,079 --> 01:08:12,169
Didn’t you see what happened to the people of Thamood(ثمود),

834
01:08:12,454 --> 01:08:15,300
aren’t you afraid that the same fate will befall you.

835
01:08:16,040 --> 01:08:21,139
He is reminding them about what happens to you when you are living a life of luxury.

836
01:08:23,612 --> 01:08:29,911
Alright, we'll close with that and we'll carry on In Sha Allah(إن شاء الله) next week.

837
01:08:30,766 --> 01:08:37,060
We'll continue talking about the finances of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه), financial issues.

838
01:08:37,406 --> 01:08:43,934
We'll also talk about the judicial system in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه,

839
01:08:44,869 --> 01:08:51,174
and that will probably take us a few days and then we'll move on to the Ghazawaat(غزوات),

840
01:08:51,588 --> 01:08:57,379
the Ghazawaat(غزوات) will be the last thing, we'll talk about Ghazawaat(غزوات) of Al-Iraq,

841
01:08:58,747 --> 01:09:02,812
 Iran and As-Sham(ألشام) and Egypt.

842
01:09:05,969 --> 01:09:07,949
Tayeb(طيب), some of the questions.

